Signed-off-by: Herbert Xu <herbert@gondor.apana.org.au>

Here is the root cause:
In krb5enc_dispatch_decrypt(), the skcipher callback was set to req->base.complete (the caller's completion handler) instead of an intermediate callback that chains into hash verification. As a result, when the skcipher completes asynchronously, the request is completed directly without executing krb5enc_dispatch_decrypt_hash(), bypassing integrity verification.

Here is the patch:

